Ludion had nothing on this, so I checked the web. **The answer depends on your version.** In current releases, the `fetchMock` export from `cloudflare:test` is gone.

## Current versions (Vitest 4 integration): `fetchMock` is removed

Cloudflare's Vitest 3 → 4 migration guide says: *"The `import { fetchMock } from "cloudflare:test"` import has been removed."* It doesn't give a replacement API. Instead, it says to mock `globalThis.fetch` yourself or use a library such as MSW.

Mocking `globalThis.fetch` directly:

```ts
import { env, exports } from "cloudflare:workers";
import { afterEach, expect, it, vi } from "vitest";

afterEach(() => vi.restoreAllMocks());

it("mocks an upstream call", async () => {
  vi.spyOn(globalThis, "fetch").mockImplementation(async (input, init) => {
    const req = new Request(input, init);
    if (req.url === "https://api.example.com/users/1") {
      return Response.json({ id: 1, name: "Ada" });
    }
    throw new Error(`Unexpected fetch: ${req.method} ${req.url}`);
  });

  const res = await exports.default.fetch("https://my-worker/user/1");
  expect(await res.json()).toEqual({ id: 1, name: "Ada" });
});
```

- **Same isolate only:** the spy catches fetches made by Worker code running in the test isolate, which is the default for the integration.
- **MSW instead:** if you'd rather use MSW, the migration guide links to a request-mocking example in the `workers-sdk` repo. Copy its setup from there; the guide itself has no MSW code.
- **Unconfirmed rename:** some third-party posts say the package was renamed to `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin` (1.0) and now uses `msw` plus `@msw/cloudflare` for mocking. I couldn't confirm that in Cloudflare's own docs. Check the official changelog before you install anything based on it.

## Older versions: the legacy `fetchMock` API

`fetchMock` was an undici `MockAgent`:

```ts
import { fetchMock, SELF } from "cloudflare:test";
import { beforeAll, afterEach, it, expect } from "vitest";

beforeAll(() => {
  fetchMock.activate();
  fetchMock.disableNetConnect(); // throw on any fetch that wasn't mocked
});
afterEach(() => fetchMock.assertNoPendingInterceptors());

it("mocks an upstream call", async () => {
  fetchMock
    .get("https://api.example.com")
    .intercept({ path: "/users/1", method: "GET" })
    .reply(200, JSON.stringify({ id: 1, name: "Ada" }), {
      headers: { "content-type": "application/json" },
    });

  const res = await SELF.fetch("https://my-worker/user/1");
  expect(await res.json()).toEqual({ id: 1, name: "Ada" });
});
```

Release notes for `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` 0.20.0 list a `fetchMock` Miniflare override option as removed, with `outboundService` named as its replacement. If you're on 0.20.0 or later, check the official docs before relying on any of this.

If you tell me which package and version you're on (it's in `package.json`), I can give you the exact setup for it.

Sources:
- [Migrate from Vitest 3 to Vitest 4 (Cloudflare docs)](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/testing/vitest-integration/migration-guides/migrate-from-vitest-3-to-vitest-4/)
- [Test APIs (Cloudflare docs)](https://developers.cloudflare.com:2053/workers/testing/vitest-integration/test-apis)
- [vitest-pool-workers 0.20.0 release notes](https://newreleases.io/project/github/cloudflare/workers-sdk/release/@cloudflare%2Fvitest-pool-workers@0.20.0)
- [releases.sh: 0.20.0 Miniflare override options pruned](https://releases.sh/release/rel_a7C6TTOpRodtIVBmBlw9o)
- [eCorpIT: vitest-plugin rename and MSW mocking](https://ecorpit.com/cloudflare-vitest-plugin-1-0-msw-peer-dependency-conflict-2026/)
- [eCorpIT: vitest-plugin v1 migration gaps](https://ecorpit.com/cloudflare-vitest-plugin-v1-rename-msw-mocking-codemod-gaps-2026/)
- [Mintlify mirror of the vitest-pool-workers docs (older fetchMock usage)](https://www.mintlify.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/api/vitest-pool-workers)

